    "teacher_markdown": "**Intent:** This level is about applying their newfound content knowledge to interpret unclear directions. Students may need multiple prompts to complete the level \\- encourage them to evaluate their results and iterate until the result matches their expectations.\r\n\r\nThe vision descriptions are intentionally written in non-technical language (\"I want it to feel like two separate parts,\" \"like something you'd hang on a wall\") \\- students have to translate that language into precise HTML/CSS prompts. This translation is a core skill.\r\n\r\n**Circulation questions:**\r\n\r\n- \"What specific language did you use in your prompts that you didn't use before?\"  \r\n- \"How many times did you iterate? What changed between your first attempt and your last?\"\r\n\r\n**Expected mistakes and misconceptions:**\r\n\r\n- Students may write very general prompts (\"make it look nice\") and be surprised when the result doesn't match \\- ask them to find one specific thing in the vision description and translate it into a CSS property they know  \r\n- Students may feel like they \"failed\" if they needed many iterations \\- explicitly reframe: \"needing four tries means you were paying attention four times. That's the skill.\"  \r\n- Students may treat the target screenshot as the only valid answer \\- remind them the instructions say \"it doesn't need to be identical, just similar enough\"",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "true"
  },
